  ('e1b99153-0102-47fc-b0cd-c21509827b0b', 'Side Plank', 'Abs', 'Works your obliques and helps stabilize your spine. Lie on your side and support your body between your forearm and knee to your feet.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'http://www.bodybuilding.com/', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/580/view/'),
  ('22148472-4947-4124-96f6-f06c008ed867', 'Side Plank (Custom)', 'Calves', 'Hold a side plank on your elbow, keep pelvis, ribcage and spine aligned in one straight line, breathe normally, avoid sagging the hips or shrugging the shoulder.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2754/view/'),
  ('5e2761cf-839e-435e-bedb-35e132dcb5ce', 'Side plank right', 'Abs', 'Starting position:
Lie down on your side, with your bottom elbow at a right angle, arm sticking out. Lift your pelvis off the floor by lifting your bottom shoulder up, keeping the forearm on the floor; your head, pelvis, and feet should be in a straight line.
Steps:
- Hold this position.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', null, 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1019/view/'),
  ('cd7bbafc-4092-4194-aa20-e380f1fe45f0', 'Side Slides + Squats', 'Quads', 'With feet a little wider than shoulder-width apart and staying low to mimic a defensive position, you should step with their lead leg and push off with their plant leg.
After three slides, rotate your body for 180 degree on the guiding (/outer) leg and do a squat. Continue.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Insight', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1195/view/'),
  ('9801e20b-69c3-43d0-9066-450a68230c42', 'Side split squats left', null, 'Starting position:
- Stand tall and take a wide lateral stride, just greater than shoulder width.
Steps:
- Bend one knee until your thigh is parallel to the floor. The bent knee must be in line with the foot.
- Push back to the starting position.
- Repeat.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', null, 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/986/view/'),
  ('fa9838ed-84e8-476c-8157-1774a9c90aff', 'Side split squats right', null, 'Starting position:
- Stand tall and take a wide lateral stride, just greater than shoulder width.
Steps:
